===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁ers-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|errour}}, from {{der|en|xno|errour}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|error}}, from {{der|en|la|error|t=wandering about|pos=noun}}, derived from the verb {{m|la|errō|t=to wander, to err}}. Cognate with {{cog|got|𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌶𐌴𐌹|t=error}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌶𐌾𐌰𐌽|t=to lead astray}}. More at {{l|en|err}}. {{surf|en|err|-or<pos:suffix forming nouns of quality, state, or condition>}}. Displaced native {{noncog|ang|dwield||error}}.

